Patches to the Android Open Source Project
------------------------------------------
The files in runtime/aosp/patches/ are modifications to source code of the Android Open
Source Project (art, libcore, frameworks/base and external/icu, at the tag named in
scripts/fetch-aosp.sh). They are derivative works of that code and are provided under the
licenses of the files they modify: the Apache License, Version 2.0, for art and
frameworks/base; the licenses stated in each file for libcore (Apache-2.0, and GPL-2.0 with
the Classpath exception for the parts that come from OpenJDK) and for ICU (the Unicode
License).

Software that is downloaded, not included
-----------------------------------------
This repository contains no third-party code or binaries. The build scripts download the
following to the machine they run on, each under its own license:

  Android Open Source Project sources      android.googlesource.com   Apache-2.0 and others
    art, libcore, libbase, liblog, libziparchive, libnativehelper, frameworks/base (parts),
    frameworks/native (headers), bionic (headers), and the external projects icu,
    boringssl, conscrypt, expat, fdlibm, dlmalloc, musl, lz4, lzma, fmtlib, tinyxml2,
    cpu_features
  Android 15 emulator system image         dl.google.com              Android SDK terms
    used for the boot class path jars, ICU data, time zone data and root certificates
  Robolectric android-all and              Maven Central              Apache-2.0 / MIT
    nativeruntime-dist-compat                                         (fonts: OFL, Apache-2.0)
    the Android framework classes and resources, AOSP's host build of the framework's
    native graphics code, and system fonts
  R8/D8                                    Google Maven               Apache-2.0

An IPA produced by this tool contains code built from those components together with the
Android app that was converted. Whoever distributes such an IPA is responsible for
complying with the licenses of everything inside it, including the app's own.

